      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "`KeystoreSecretVault.seal` initializes a `Cipher` with a Keystore key to seal values. RVSec reported that it did not observe a generator for the key passed to `Cipher.init`, which its rule expects.\n\nI leave that call unchanged and give each tier in `getOrCreateKey` its own `KeyGenerator` for initialization and generation. This also resolves the reported `KeyGenerator` call-sequence violation in `getOrCreateKey`. Existing keys are still reused, provider acquisition remains outside the retry catch, and tier failures retain their fallback handling.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
